            "section": "IV.B"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "LNG carriers are priced at the LNG terminal tariff (section DD) instead of the port's general rates. Berth hire and anchorage are printed per GT per hour (or per day at the LNG terminal) without 'or part thereof', so exact time is used. Calls at the single point mooring and the crude oil (VLCC) jetty are charged by contract and are not priced.",
          "source": {
            "document": "bpts-2026-06-15",
            "page": 42
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The environment protection charge applies to bulk, break-bulk, liquid, Ro-Ro and gas carriers, ships at the MICT (DP World) container berths and ships calling for other activities. It is not applied to container ships at the other container terminals.",
          "source": {
            "document": "bpts-2026-06-15",
            "page": 31
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The circular that introduced the fuel surcharge applies it 'for all the vessel coming at Mundra port', so LNG carriers pay it too. (Hazira's tariff, by contrast, exempts LNG ships.)",
